    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0940" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg844"/>

                <head>No. 374.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mathews to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1879-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            21, 1879</date>. (Received September 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your circular dispatch No. 13, under date of 10th June last, the instructions of
                    which will be carefully complied with.</p>
                <p>I beg to inclose herewith for your information a copy of my reply, transmitted to
                    Mr. Wines, president of the International Penitentiary Commission, to his letter
                    requesting information on the state of prisons, and the administration of
                    criminal justice, &amp;c., in Morocco.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FELIX A. MATHEWS.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d403-a1.xml" xpointer="d403-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
